frames, Python/R packages, reproducible workflows, and version control), univariate and multivariate statistical analysis of small and medium-size datasets, regression methods, hypothesis testing, probability models, basic supervised and unsupervised machine learning, data visualization, and network analysis. Students will learn how to use data to make effective arguments in a way that promotes the ethical usage of data. Students who complete the course will be able to produce meaningful, data-driven analyses of real-world problems and will be prepared to begin more advanced work in data-intensive domains.", "catalogBreadth": null, "catalogDistr": null, "catalogEnrollmentPriority": "", "catalogLang": null, "catalogForbiddenOverlaps": null, "catalogAttribute": null, "catalogWhenOffered": null, "catalogComments": null, "catalogPrereqCoreq": null, "catalogPrereq": "one course is core statistics (MATH 1710 or equivalent) and one course in core programming (CS 1110 or CS 1112) or permission of instructor.", "catalogCoreq": "", "catalogFee": null, "catalogSatisfiesReq": null, "catalogPermission": null, "catalogCourseSubfield": null, "catalogOutcomes": null, "acadCareer": "UG", "acadGroup": "EN", "catalogName": null, "catalogNextOffered": null, "lastTermsOffered": "2026SU, 2025FA, 2024FA, 2024SU", "catalogCredits": null, "catalogGradeOption": null, "catalogLocation": null, "catalogCrosslisted": null, "catalogCrosslistings": null, "catalogComeets": null, "exploreCriteriaIds": []}, {"strm": 2930, "crseId": 352898, "crseOfferNbr": 2, "subject": "INFO", "catalogNbr": "3200", "titleShort": "Tech, Behavior, and Society", "titleLong": "Technology, Behavior and Society", "crseAttrs": [{"crseAttr": "0012", "crseAttrValue": "CA-AG", "descr": "AG-Cultural Analysis", "descrformal": "AG-Cultural Analysis", "attrDescr": "Distribution Requirements", "attrDescrShort": "DistReq"}], "crseAttrValueGroups": [{"attrDescr": "Distribution Requirements", "crseAttrValues": "(CA-AG)"}], "enrollGrou